# Requisições de exemplo para testar a API à mão.
# Use a extensão "REST Client" do VS Code (humao.rest-client): clique em
# "Send Request" acima de cada bloco. Rode na ordem — os blocos usam o id
# devolvido pelos anteriores.

@api = http://127.0.0.1:3333/api

### Índice da API
GET {{api}}

### Saúde
GET {{api}}/health

############################################################ Vagas

### Cadastrar vaga manual
# @name createJob
POST {{api}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Desenvolvedor Full Stack Júnior",
  "company": "Empresa Exemplo",
  "url": "https://empresa.gupy.io/jobs/123?utm_source=linkedin",
  "location": "Campinas, SP",
  "workModel": "hybrid",
  "contractType": "clt",
  "seniority": "junior",
  "stack": ["TypeScript", "NestJS", "React", "PostgreSQL"],
  "salaryMin": 3500,
  "salaryMax": 4500,
  "salaryCurrency": "BRL",
  "salaryPeriod": "month",
  "postedAt": "2026-10-05"
}

### Listar (padrão: inbox + salvas)
GET {{api}}/jobs?limit=20

### Filtrar
GET {{api}}/jobs?q=full&workModel=remote,hybrid&stack=nestjs&postedWithinDays=30

### Detalhe
GET {{api}}/jobs/{{createJob.response.body.id}}

### Editar (null limpa o campo)
PATCH {{api}}/jobs/{{createJob.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Indicação do Pedro. Falar com a Ana do RH.",
  "location": null
}

############################################################ Triagem

### Salvar
PUT {{api}}/jobs/{{createJob.response.body.id}}/triage
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "saved" }

### Descartar com motivo (desfazer = "inbox")
# PUT {{api}}/jobs/<id>/triage
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "status": "dismissed", "reason": "presencial" }

### Ver descartadas
GET {{api}}/jobs?triage=dismissed

############################################################ Candidaturas

### Candidatar-se
# @name apply
POST {{api}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobId": "{{createJob.response.body.id}}",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-06T10:00:00-03:00",
  "appliedVia": "Gupy",
  "salaryExpectation": 4000
}

### Registrar evento (data retroativa vale)
POST {{api}}/applications/{{apply.response.body.id}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in_process",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-08",
  "note": "Entrevista com RH"
}

### Próxima etapa
PATCH {{api}}/applications/{{apply.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nextStepAt": "2026-10-15T14:00:00-03:00",
  "nextStepNote": "Entrevista técnica com o time"
}

### Detalhe com linha do tempo
GET {{api}}/applications/{{apply.response.body.id}}

### Listar e resumo por status
GET {{api}}/applications?status=applied,in_process

###
GET {{api}}/applications/summary

############################################################ Currículo

### Currículo (cria as seções padrão no 1º acesso)
# @name resume
GET {{api}}/resume

### Preencher o 1º campo da 2ª seção (Contato > E-mail)
PATCH {{api}}/resume/items/{{resume.response.body.sections[1].items[0].id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "label": "E-mail", "value": "voce@email.com" } }

### Adicionar experiência (5ª seção = Experiência)
POST {{api}}/resume/sections/{{resume.response.body.sections[4].id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "data": {
    "title": "Desenvolvedor Full Stack Trainee",
    "organization": "Empresa",
    "location": "Americana, SP",
    "startDate": "2026-01",
    "current": true,
    "description": "APIs em NestJS, app em React Native, PostgreSQL e Docker."
  }
}

### Nova seção
POST {{api}}/resume/sections
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Voluntariado", "kind": "entries" }

### Exportar em texto puro
GET {{api}}/resume/export

############################################################ Descoberta

### Fontes ativas e última execução
GET {{api}}/discovery/sources

### Buscar agora (todas as fontes, termos do .env)
POST {{api}}/discovery/scan

### Buscar agora com termos próprios
POST {{api}}/discovery/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sources": ["gupy"], "terms": ["nestjs", "react native"] }

### Histórico de execuções
GET {{api}}/discovery/runs?limit=10

### Vagas que vieram da Gupy
GET {{api}}/jobs?source=gupy&limit=20

############################################################ Preferências e nota
# docs/features/07-preferences-score.md — a nota é calculada em segundo plano.

### Preferências atuais
GET {{api}}/preferences

### Salvar preferências (exemplo: perfil do autor — ajuste e rode)
PUT {{api}}/preferences
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stacksCore": ["node.js", "nestjs", "react", "typescript"],
  "stacksPlus": ["react native", "postgresql", "docker"],
  "stacksAvoid": ["php", "delphi"],
  "seniorities": ["intern", "trainee", "junior"],
  "workModels": ["remote", "hybrid"],
  "cities": ["Americana", "Campinas", "Sumaré", "Santa Bárbara d'Oeste", "Nova Odessa"],
  "contractTypes": ["clt", "pj", "internship"],
  "maxAgeDays": 30,
  "minMonthlySalary": null,
  "blockedCompanies": []
}

### Desligar a nota (lista volta a sair por data)
PUT {{api}}/preferences
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Tecnologias conhecidas e quantas vagas citam cada uma
GET {{api}}/preferences/stacks

### Recalcular todas as notas (segundo plano)
POST {{api}}/preferences/rescore

### Vagas pela nota (padrão quando há preferências)
GET {{api}}/jobs?limit=20

### Só as boas, sem incompatíveis
GET {{api}}/jobs?minScore=700&hideIncompatible=true

### Pela data de entrada, mesmo com preferências
GET {{api}}/jobs?sort=recent&limit=20
